{"_id":"68a736128ec3d8323af14ca3","nodeId":"c1dadtQgbqXwcsQhI6de0","roadmapSlug":"data-engineer","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:58.672Z","description":"# Distributed Systems\n\nA distributed system is a collection of independent computers that communicate and coordinate to appear as a single unified system. They are widely used for scalability, fault tolerance, and high availability in modern applications. However, they bring challenges such as synchronization, consistency trade-offs (CAP theorem), concurrency, and network latency.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Introduction to Distributed Systems","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/a-thorough-introduction-to-distributed-systems-3b91562c9b3c/","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf5258"},{"type":"article","title":"Distributed Systems Guide","url":"https://www.baeldung.com/cs/distributed-systems-guide","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf5259"},{"type":"video","title":"Distributed Systems Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IJWwfMyPu1c","_id":"6a7f4a42cb44947debcf525a"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:58.294Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0417044","title":"DataCamp - Associate Data Engineer in SQL","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/WOP6XG"},{"_id":"6a5e04e1fb5fcb94d0417100","title":"DataCamp - Data Engineer in Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/JkYLbr"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/data-engineer/content/c1dadtQgbqXwcsQhI6de0.md"}